WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.176
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.476 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:16.180
Unit one: IELTS Overview and Band Scores. Today you will understand the four IELTS papers and how band scores work.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.982
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.933 --> 00:00:23.340
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:25.312
Band score.

7
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:30.000
Band score means a number from 0 to 9 showing your level.

8
00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:32.954
I need a band score of 6.5.

9
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.574
Your turn. Say: Band score.

10
00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:40.771
Band score.

11
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:42.599
Academic.

12
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:46.802
Academic means the test version for university study.

13
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:49.103
I take IELTS Academic.

14
00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:52.230
Your turn. Say: Academic.

15
00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.161
Academic.

16
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.080
General Training.

17
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:02.012
General Training means the version for work and migration.

18
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:04.210
She chose General Training.

19
00:01:04.817 --> 00:01:07.678
Your turn. Say: General Training.

20
00:01:10.533 --> 00:01:11.941
General Training.

21
00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:13.696
Module.

22
00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:17.217
Module means one of the four test papers.

23
00:01:17.817 --> 00:01:19.433
Listening is the first module.

24
00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:22.982
Your turn. Say: Module.

25
00:01:25.833 --> 00:01:26.695
Module.

26
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.136
Overall score.

27
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.380
Overall score means the average of the four band scores.

28
00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:35.913
My overall score is 7.

29
00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:39.401
Your turn. Say: Overall score.

30
00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:43.848
Overall score.

31
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:45.596
Descriptor.

32
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.616
Descriptor means a short sentence that explains a band.

33
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:52.019
Read each band descriptor.

34
00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:55.455
Your turn. Say: Descriptor.

35
00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.046
Descriptor.

36
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:00.866
Proficiency.

37
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:04.697
Proficiency means how well you can use a language.

38
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:07.236
Test your English proficiency.

39
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.618
Your turn. Say: Proficiency.

40
00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:14.561
Proficiency.

41
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:16.225
Candidate.

42
00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:19.878
Candidate means a person who takes the test.

43
00:02:20.483 --> 00:02:22.251
Each candidate gets a number.

44
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.491
Your turn. Say: Candidate.

45
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:29.218
Candidate.

46
00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:33.603
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.007
Visal, why do students take IELTS?

48
00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:50.637
Many students need a band score for university or work abroad. The test has four modules: Listening, Reading, Writing and Speaking, and each one gets its own band score.

49
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:53.970
How is the overall score decided?

50
00:02:55.083 --> 00:03:10.193
Examiners average the four band scores and round to the nearest half band. For example, 6.5, 7.0, 6.0 and 7.0 gives an overall 6.5.

51
00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:14.479
What is the difference between Academic and General Training?

52
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:27.872
Listening and Speaking are the same. In Reading and Writing, Academic uses university-style texts and charts, while General Training uses everyday and work topics.

53
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:30.429
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:31.283 --> 00:03:35.733
Grammar focus: Strategy: know the test before you practise.

55
00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.219
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:42.923
Listening, Reading, Writing and Speaking each count equally in the overall score.

57
00:03:43.817 --> 00:03:48.800
A 6.5 overall is the average of four bands, rounded to the nearest half.

58
00:03:49.733 --> 00:03:56.890
Know your target band, then study the descriptors for that band in each module. Practise all four modules because each counts the same.

59
00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:01.661
Be careful! Don't say: Overall score is the highest band.

60
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.180
Say: Overall score is the average of four.

61
00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.387
The overall is the average.

62
00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.713
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:13.919
Choosing My Target.

64
00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:17.031
Amara wants to study nursing in Australia.

65
00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:21.879
Her university asks for an overall band of 6.5.

66
00:04:22.867 --> 00:04:26.364
She also needs at least 6.0 in every module.

67
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.202
She checks the band descriptors for Writing and Speaking.

68
00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.268
Then she makes a weekly plan for all four modules.

69
00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:39.357
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:40.217 --> 00:04:42.263
How many modules does IELTS have?

71
00:04:42.563 --> 00:04:45.694
A, four. B, two. C, three.

72
00:04:49.233 --> 00:04:50.850
The answer is A: four.

73
00:04:51.983 --> 00:04:54.784
The overall score is the blank of the four bands.

74
00:04:55.084 --> 00:04:58.552
A, highest. B, lowest. C, average.

75
00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.285
The answer is C: average.

76
00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.680
Which paper is different in Academic and General Training?

77
00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:12.448
A, Listening. B, Reading. C, Speaking.

78
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.000
The answer is B: Reading.

79
00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.451
Amara checks the band blank for Writing.

80
00:05:21.751 --> 00:05:25.765
A, modules. B, descriptors. C, candidates.

81
00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.752
The answer is B: descriptors.

82
00:05:32.917 --> 00:05:35.137
What does Amara need in every module?

83
00:05:35.437 --> 00:05:41.203
A, at least 8.0. B, at least 5.0. C, at least 6.0.

84
00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:48.067
The answer is C: at least 6.0.

85
00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:52.291
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.475
What band score do you need, and why?

87
00:06:04.283 --> 00:06:05.784
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:06:06.084 --> 00:06:25.782
I need an overall band score of 6.5 because I want to study at a university abroad. I also need at least 6.0 in every module. First I will read the band descriptors for each module, and then I will practise all four skills every week.

89
00:06:26.082 --> 00:06:27.780
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:28.683 --> 00:06:34.169
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: know the test before you practise.

91
00:06:34.469 --> 00:06:38.909
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:39.209 --> 00:06:41.815
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

93
00:06:42.115 --> 00:06:45.951
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

